  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Late-inning rallies keep this team alive when it matters most.",
    "what_this_means": "Campusano supplied the power that tied the game in the ninth. A two-RBI night in a lineup that managed six hits and six strikeouts. Walker Buehler held New York to one run across five innings, setting the frame for whatever came late. The bullpen didn't just survive; Matsui, Rodriguez, Morejon, and Miller combined to blank the Yankees for five straight innings after the starter left. That's the infrastructure that wins one-run games. Campusano's tenth-inning home run was the finish, but it was built on a staff that refused to fold after giving up early contact. This is a team that doesn't need a lead to win. Just enough time for the right swing to find them. The formula works until the bats don't answer.",
    "what_to_watch": "Rod\u00f3n takes the mound tonight for New York with a 3.20 ERA. Ray has been sharp lately, posting a 2.56 ERA over his last four starts. He'll need that form against an offense still capable of one big inning.",
